course: dictionary
lesson: 5342
title: The kicker
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A kicker is a person, or sometimes an animal, that kicks. In sport, the kicker is the player who kicks the ball, often to score points. The kenning says «A kenning describes something with two-word phrases, such as "ball-kicker" for a footballer», so a ball-kicker is a footballer.
explain: Look at the ending. Kicker comes from kick, and the ending -er often means someone who does the action, just as goal-scorer means someone who scores goals. If you know kick, you can work out kicker.
explain: Kicker also has an everyday meaning. «And here's the kicker…» tells you a surprise is coming at the end, and it is often an unpleasant one. The clue is the way the sentence builds up to something, so read the words before and after it.
fact: A kicker is a person or animal that kicks.
fact: In rugby and American football, the kicker is the player who kicks to score points.
fact: The ending -er often means someone who does the action, as in kicker, scorer or singer.
fact: «Kicker» (informal) means a surprising twist or extra fact at the end, often an unpleasant one.
fact: In a kenning, «ball-kicker» is a two-word name for a footballer.
exercise: «The team's kicker lined up the ball and kicked it between the posts.» What is a kicker? | A referee who blows the whistle | A goal that is scored | * A player who kicks the ball | A ball made of leather
exercise: In the kenning «ball-kicker», what does the phrase describe? | A bird that flies | A wooden ball | * A footballer | A goalpost
exercise: «And here's the kicker…» What does kicker mean here? | A tall tree | * A surprise twist at the end | A sports game | A large boot
test: «The donkey was a notorious kicker, so nobody went near its back legs.» What does kicker mean? | * An animal that kicks | A cart | A tall tree | A quiet farmer
test: Which of these is a kicker in rugby? | * A player who kicks the ball to score | A referee | The crowd in the stands | A goalpost
exam: «The story seemed happy, but the kicker at the end was a shock.» What does kicker mean? | * An unexpected, often unpleasant surprise at the end | A goal scored in the last minute | The last word on the page | A kick on the leg
